# Stage an attack of opportunity against an acid blob and read the A_DEQU
# confirmation prompt the AoO raises (bd inc-hy9u, inc-m2zi edit 12).
#
#   INCURSION_AOO_PROBE=1 INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/dequ-aoo-prompt.keys 5
#
# WHAT IS BEING MEASURED. Creature::OAttack (src/Fight.cpp) calls
# ConfirmDequAttack before it resolves the blow. For a player with
# OPT_WARN_DEQU on, striking a monster whose A_DEQU risks the weapon, that
# helper asks "Attack the <monster> (". No key script can make a MONSTER
# provoke an AoO, so the prompt has never been seen on an AoO. The probe
# INCURSION_AOO_PROBE (AoOProbeArrange, src/Player.cpp) closes the gap: it
# reads the eight squares beside the player and, the first tick a hostile
# A_DEQU monster stands in one, calls that monster's ProvokeAoO(), which
# offers the player his attack of opportunity.
#
# THE WEAPON MUST NOT BE MAGICAL. The setup's starting weapon is an orcish
# dagger +1, and for a magical item the blob's 2d4 acid cannot beat hardness
# and ConfirmDequAttack returns quietly. So, as dequ-hardness-plain.keys does,
# an ordinary (non-magical) long sword is bought and swapped into the Weapon
# Hand first: edit 5 bypasses hardness for a non-magical item, so its A_DEQU
# damage reaches the prompt.
#
# The blob is summoned east of the player. The prompt is declined with 'n':
# this check reads the prompt, not the strike.
#
# Read by tools/check_dequ_aoo_prompt.sh. Its evidence is logs/aoo.log (the
# probe staged an AoO) and the aoo-prompt screen dump (the prompt was shown).
@include dequ-setup.keys

w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*9                 # walk the glyph row to ordinary weapons
@until "Long sword" DOWN
DOWN                    # the wanted row is the middle of three; step onto it
ENTER
b                       # Weapon Hand -- the slot lettering skips 'd' (Drop)
SPACE                   # swap the sword into it
@while "two-handed" n
s                       # stow the starting knife the swap pushed into the air
@until "SPACE:Swap" i    # the inventory manager, if it is not already open
@until ">>b)Weapon" b    # select the Weapon Hand
@until "base value of" x # Examine: confirms the ordinary sword is wielded
@dump:armed
@until "Things in View" ESC

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Jellies"
@choose "acid blob"
RIGHT ENTER             # summon it east of the player
@dump:summoned
.                       # wait one turn; the probe fires at the next tick
@until "Attack the" .   # if the prompt is not up yet, wait it out
@dump:aoo-prompt
n                       # decline: the check only needs the prompt shown
@dump:after
@quit
